$join_stems — mix sounds[] stems into one WAV

SUMMARY
  Loads every sound in sounds[], sums them (typical stem recombination), and
  writes one mixed WAV to sounds[].

SYNTAX
  $join_stems
  $join_stems(normalize=1, sample_rate=44100)

INPUT
  sounds[] — required; two or more stem files (WAV/MP3). One file passes through.

OUTPUT
  sounds[] — single joined WAV.

ARGUMENTS
  normalize= — scale mix to avoid clipping when sum exceeds 1.0 (default 1).
  sample_rate= — decode/resample rate in Hz (default 44100).

REQUIREMENTS
  soundfile or ffmpeg (same as $music_separation). Runs in .venvs/media.

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_JOIN_STEMS=1 — stub WAV text without audio deps.

EXAMPLE
  @mix: (
    $select(sounds=[0]) -> $change_voice,
    stems% -> $select(sounds=[1])
  ) -> $join_stems -> $save('output.wav')

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No.
